60% more than normal cost is 60% of $120. 60% of $120 is (60/100) * 120 = 0.6 * 120 = $72. So the increased cost is $72. The normal cost is $120 per month. So total cost per month is $120 + $72 = $192. To find the cost per year, we multiply the monthly cost by 12: $192 * 12 = $2304.

Thus, he pays $2304 a year.
\boxed{2304}

